{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788132778,"nonce":"NUh5CwpEe7HxFRauvWPbBH95W60=","title":"Wave 3 — hands. Depends: 1.1 (protocol), 2.4 (bills are read there). Gates M1.","message":"Filed session 4 after TWO independent audits — a decompiled action-surface sweep\nand a sweep of the game's own learning-helper curriculum — converged on this as\nthe single largest hole in the action model.\n\n\n**Nothing in 3.1–3.5 can create a production bill.** 2.4 READS bills; 3.4 covers\nonly medical bills on a pawn. So the colony can have a stove and never cook.\n\nThe convergence is the argument. The action-surface audit found it by\nenumerating `BillStack`. The curriculum audit found it independently, because\nthe scripted tutorial's step 11 is \"add a cook-simple-meal bill, target ~10\",\nand its text is explicit: *\"once a bill has been created, colonists will do the\nwork automatically\"* — nothing happens otherwise.\n\nAnd the symptom is already on our own bench: `Alert_NeedMealSource` checks for a\nmeal-source BUILDING (`def.building.isMealSource`), not a live bill, so \"stove\nbuilt, no bill, nobody cooks\" has no dedicated alert. It surfaces only when\n`Alert_LowFood` eventually trips — by which time the colony is already hungry.\n4.3's scope line says \"food (grow/hunt/**cook** or stocked)\"; cook is currently\nunreachable, so M1 either dodges into stocked meals or fails.\n\n\n**Bills**\n- `add` / `remove` / `reorder` / `suspend` on any `IBillGiver`.\n  `BillUtility.MakeNewBill` (`RimWorld/BillUtility.cs:36`) → `BillStack.AddBill`\n  (`RimWorld/BillStack.cs:69`).\n- Repeat modes and counts: `Bill_Production` fields at `:12,14,22,24,26,40`.\n  `suspended` (`Bill.cs:29`) is distinct from paused — expose both honestly.\n- Store mode: `Bill_Production.SetStoreMode` (`:197`). The backing fields are\n  private, so the setter is mandatory, not a convenience.\n- Worker restriction: the mutually-exclusive quartet at `Bill.cs:165,173,181,189`.\n- Ingredient filter: seeded from `recipe.defaultIngredientFilter` in the ctor\n  (`Bill.cs:156`), so \"any raw food\" costs zero calls — do not rebuild it.\n\n**Storage settings** (same file because they share `IStoreSettingsParent`, and\nbecause a bill without a place to put its output is half a verb)\n- Filters and priority for `Zone_Stockpile` AND `Building_Storage` — shelves,\n  crates, graves, bookcases, turret shell filters.\n- Priority MUST go through the property (`RimWorld/StorageSettings.cs:23`); the\n  setter is where haul-manager invalidation lives.\n- **Trap:** a grouped `Building_Storage.GetStoreSettings()` returns the GROUP's\n  object (`RimWorld/Building_Storage.cs:100`), so writing `building.settings`\n  while grouped silently edits a shadowed object. `StorageGroupUtility\n  .SetStorageGroup` (`:163`) is the one mutator for linking.\n- `StorageSettingsClipboard` (`:16,:23,:29`) gives copy/paste for free.\n\n\n**The gate lives in the widget — see DESIGN §Action model.** `AddBill` checks\nNOTHING: not `RecipeDef.AvailableNow` (`Verse/RecipeDef.cs:241`), not\n`AvailableOnNow` (`:398`), not the 15-bill cap (`BillStack.cs:15`). This verb\nreproduces those checks and cites each one in a comment, or it is a god-hand.\n\n`BillStack.Reorder` (`:87`) checks only the lower bound; an offset past the end\nthrows out of `List.Insert`. Clamp it.\n\nEvery mutation echoes evidence and journals, per DESIGN.\n\n\nWhether bill identity is index or a stable id (rwtest needs to name a bill\nacross a save/load); how much of the ingredient filter surface to expose in v1\nversus a \"sane default\" argument; whether storage settings deserve their own\nverb namespace rather than riding with bills.\n\n\n- On a colony with a stove and raw food and no bills: add a repeat-forever\n  cook-simple-meal bill, advance, and demonstrate meals existing that did not\n  before — the full loop, not just that the bill object appeared.\n- A bill for a recipe whose research is not done is REFUSED with the game's own\n  reason, not queued. This is the invariant above and the reason the spec exists.\n- Reorder past the end returns `bad-args` rather than throwing.\n- Setting a priority on a grouped `Building_Storage` is visible through the\n  group, demonstrating the shadowed-object trap was avoided.\n- Zero red errors.","files":null}]}